# Client Order Place speed (busy dinner)

## Feel targets
| Action | Target |
|--------|--------|
| Button first response | Instant (&lt;50ms visual) |
| Add item | &lt;150ms on screen |
| Open table → order | &lt;300ms feel |
| Category switch | &lt;100ms |
| Send to kitchen | UI instant; Mother can finish after |
| Open Restaurant | Tables visible immediately from cache |
| Sync / Update All | Till stays usable |

## Architecture — silent live till
- **UI reads SQLite only** (warm last-good). Never wait on Mother to paint.
- **Mother → SQLite** via WebSocket (primary) + quiet safety-net pull (~45s) while logged in.
- Sync/preloaders/toasts are **silent when cache is warm**. Loader/toast only for cold/empty or explicit Update All / hard failure.
- Client → Mother HTTP for order mutations (no Client→cloud).
- Optimistic UI + first-tap overlay hygiene (Phases 1–4).

## Phase 1–4 — done
Optimistic Order Place · Incremental shell · Warm cache · Non-blocking sync · First-tap · Timers/ChefLoader · In-place tables

## Silent live sync — done
1. Login warm → dashboard immediately; background sync; no “Refreshing…” toast on success.
2. Restaurant warm → paint tables now; Mother pull in background; no preloader/toast.
3. Default Mother pull does **not** drive shell `IsLoading` (that was flashing Restaurant).
4. Quiet loop while logged in refreshes SQLite and patches open Restaurant/Live in place.
5. Reconnect with warm cache: no refresh toast / Syncing flash.

## Scope
- Default: `OrderWeb.Client` + SharedUI.
- Do not port Mother AppShell nav-lock / Rider / Visual Table admin.
